  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 3.1. Increased capacity of Member States to formulate and implement national employment policies in response to the COVID-19 crisis</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Led by the Ministry of Commerce, Industry and Labour (MCIL) and in consultation with various government agencies and social partners, the 2nd Samoa National Employment Policy (SNEP2) was developed and launched in 2022. The country&#x2019;s first-ever national employment policy is anchored in the ILO Employment Policy Convention, 1964 (No. 122) and makes specific reference to the COVID-19 crisis and recovery. The SNEP2 promotes and fosters equal participation and inclusion of men, women, youth, and people with special needs in socio-economic development, decision-making, and service delivery process at all levels. SNEP2 will provide overarching support to other related youth policies to promote decent employment opportunities for young people in Samoa. The ILO provided technical assistance on the first iteration of the SNEP through a series of advisory engagements with MCIL as well as tripartite partners including technical reviews and comments on the draft NEP and development of a workplan. In the review of the SNEP, the SNEP2 built on achievements and lessons learned from the SNEP and ILO provided overarching support towards the monitoring and implementation of the SNEP workplan as well as technical and financial support towards achieving key objectives with tripartite partners.</narrative>
   </description>
